    challengesLabel: THE CHALLENGES
    challenge: <p data-end="465" data-start="232"><strong data-end="252" data-start="232">Donor management</strong><br data-end="255" data-start="252"/>Without a dedicated CRM, donor history is scattered across spreadsheets and inboxes. Segmenting donors, personalizing follow-ups, or identifying strategic donors before it is too late becomes nearly impossible.</p><p data-end="699" data-start="467"><strong data-end="494" data-start="467">Fundraising &amp; campaigns</strong><br data-end="497" data-start="494"/>Coordinating multichannel fundraising campaigns — email, website, events — without an integrated tool leads to duplicates, inconsistent data, and a loss of traceability that damages donor relationships.</p><p data-end="931" data-start="701"><strong data-end="721" data-start="701">Grant management</strong><br data-end="724" data-start="721"/>Each funder has its own conditions, payment schedules, and reporting formats. Managing several grants simultaneously without a dedicated tool exposes
      the organization to compliance errors and funding delays.</p><p data-end="1137" data-start="933"><strong data-end="956" data-start="933">Fund usage tracking</strong><br data-end="959" data-start="956"/>Proving to funders that every euro is spent in line with grant objectives requires rigorous project-based analytical accounting. Without it, every audit becomes a risky exercise.</p><p data-end="1356" data-start="1139"><strong data-end="1172" data-start="1139">Impact statistics &amp; reporting</strong><br data-end="1175" data-start="1172"/>International donors and funders require accurate impact reports. Manually consolidating field data scattered across different countries takes weeks and produces unreliable reports.</p>
